Google <a href="https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/google-search-personal-intelligence-apps/">today said</a> it is making Search "more tailored" with support for connecting Google Wallet to Personal Intelligence in AI Mode.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/google-personal-intelligence.jpg" alt="" width="1757" height="988" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1079133" /><br/>
According to Google, AI Mode will be able to map financial milestones, find ways to trim spending, and get the most from credit card benefits. The feature can read information from accounts included in Google Wallet, but it can't move, manage, or invest money.<br/>
<br/>
In the coming weeks, Google plans to add connections for Google Drive and Gemini to Google Search. Google Drive will give Search access to docs, sheets, PDFs, and more, with search responses that take into account personal information.<br/>
<br/>
Gemini integration will let both the Gemini app and AI Mode in Search share context and content. Google says if you ask the Gemini app something, AI Mode will "have that foundation to build on." With today's announcement, Google says you'll start seeing more personally relevant responses based on recent search context in both AI Mode and AI Overviews. Responses that use your personal data will soon have a "Personalization" icon below them to let you see what data was used.<br/>
<br/>
AI Mode can already connect to Gmail, Calendar, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a> for customized search responses. Connecting apps to AI Mode and Search is optional, and Google doesn't turn it on by default. Services can be connected to Personal Intelligence in AI Mode by opening up Search Personalization and choosing Connected Apps.<br/>
<br/>
That section is also where you can make sure no apps are connected or disable personalization if you don't want to share additional data with Google. You'll want to go to <a href="https://www.google.com/search-personalization/">Search Personalization</a> while logged into a Google account to turn off Personalized Recommendations, Search Services history, Likes and Preferences, Personalized Ads, and other features that Google uses for data collection. Additional controls are located in the <a href="https://myactivity.google.com/activitycontrols">Personalization Settings</a>.<br/>
<br/>
If you've used Google's Gemini, you can <a href="https://myactivity.google.com/product/gemini">turn off the setting</a> to save chat history and separately prevent Google from training AI models on your content, a change that began rolling out November 16. With chat history turned off, Google still keeps your chats for around two months. The best way to minimize what Google collects is to use Google services as little as possible. Consider a <a href="https://kagi.com/pricing">search engine like Kagi</a> to pay with money instead of data.<div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/google/">Google</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/23/google-search-wallet-access/">Google Search Gets Wallet Access, With Drive Coming Soon</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/google-search-gets-wallet-access-with-drive-coming-soon.2495086/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>